The function takes rows and returns only the PUBLIC_COLUMNS from each, so the docstring can say that accurately. [tool_use propose_change {"path":"register/export.py","summary":"Add a docstring to export_comments describing its input, output, and the public-column filtering.","diff":"--- a/register/export.py\n+++ b/register/export.py\n@@ -4,6 +4,16 @@\n PUBLIC_COLUMNS = ['reference', 'address', 'comment_date', 'stance', 'comment_text']\n \n def export_comments(rows):\n+    \"\"\"Return public-facing copies of comment rows.\n+\n+    Each row is a mapping with at least the PUBLIC_COLUMNS keys. The result\n+    is a list of new dicts containing only those columns, so private fields\n+    such as objector_name, objector_email, objector_phone and internal_note\n+    are excluded from the export.\n+\n+    Raises KeyError if a row is missing any column in PUBLIC_COLUMNS.\n+    \"\"\"\n     out = []\n     for row in rows:\n         out.append({c: row[c] for c in PUBLIC_COLUMNS})\n"}]
